  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed front dormer extension, by means of its scale, siting, design, bulk and mass would be an undesirable addition to the existing dwelling. The proposal fails to preserve the existing character of the dwelling and pattern of development. As such, the cumulative impact of the proposal would cause undue harm to the character and appearance of the host dwelling and surrounding area. The proposal is therefore contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that development recognises local character and promotes good design:&nbsp;&nbsp; National Planning Policy Framework National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024) Policies D1, D4, D5 and D6 of the London Plan (March 2021) Policies DMD1, DMD5 and SP2 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan &nbsp;(September 2024); and&nbsp;The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)"
  ],
